5. Object Detection vs Object Tracking
Object Detection	Object Tracking
Detects objects independently in each frame	Maintains object identity across frames
No memory	Remembers previous detections
Outputs class and location	Outputs class, location, and tracking ID
Example: "Car detected"	Example: "Car #7 detected again"
6. Why is Tracking Needed?

YOLO processes every frame independently.

Example

Frame 1

Car

Frame 2

Car

Frame 3

Car

YOLO does not know whether this is the same car.

Tracking solves this problem.

7. What is ByteTrack?

ByteTrack is a multi-object tracking algorithm.

Its job is to

Match detections across consecutive frames
Assign unique IDs
Keep IDs consistent over time

It does not detect objects.

It only tracks detections received from YOLO.

